 end-2027 (futures contract price = 100 − expected rate, and the series runs 95.5 → 96).\n- **Central bank path:** Governor Ashby's base case is only one 25bp cut in 2027, and she said markets \"may be getting ahead of themselves.\" The market therefore prices roughly twice the easing the CMA guides to.\n- **Rate sensitivity:** The factsheet says a 50bp lower path historically lifts the basket P/E by about 1.5 points. Today's weighted forward P/E is 19x, which already reflects the market's roughly 50bp of easing. If the CMA delivers only 25bp, the P/E could fall by about 0.75 points, to roughly 18.25x. That is about a 4% de-rating.\n- **Earnings:** Consensus expects 2027 EPS growth of 14%, driven by backlog conversion at Voltaris (14% of the fund) and Tarnwell (11%). Estimates have risen 3% over the past quarter. A 14% earnings gain outweighs a 4% de-rating, so the holdings would still be up about 9–10% on a rough combination of the two.\n- **What would break it:** The P/E would have to fall by about 12% (roughly 2.3 points) to cancel the earnings growth. That would take a sharp rise in the policy path, not just the shortfall in cuts. A miss on Voltaris or Tarnwell backlog conversion would also hurt, because those two names make up 25% of the fund.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- The 1.5-point sensitivity is a historical average, not a forecast.\n- The 14% EPS figure is consensus, and I have no data on how reliable that estimate has been.\n- I did not check the options pricing. n3 covers whether the Jan-2028 calls are attractive.","ttft_ms":2472,"type":"result","duration_ms":24849,"uuid":"ec3e0143-8437-4ba8-91a4-ad4ce51c6db2","ttft_stream_ms":1633,"time_to_request_ms":256,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":12,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":23,"input_attachments":67,"input_hooks":8,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":11,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":20,"init_frame_send":15,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":13,"message_prep":0,"model_config_